    "only_first_scope_line_changed": true,
    "reviewed_invariants": [
      "Mco retains real SYSCTRL and PA8 ownership; no split, reconstructed singleton, release API, reconfiguration API, or extra source variant is introduced.",
      "Pure admission precedes hardware writes and checks initialized cycle-qualified HCLK/PCLK bounds, ordered nonzero board declarations, source range, GPIO supply/ambient/load policy, and exact rational divided ceiling.",
      "All eight unchanged divisor entries are selected from validated metadata: (0,1), (1,2), (2,8), (3,64), (4,128), (5,256), (6,512), (7,1024).",
      "Inherited non-disabled SOURCE is rejected before reserved bits and GPIO reset checks. The critical section encloses MMIO admission, programming, attachment, readbacks, and constructor error cleanup.",
      "Flex uses the existing GPIOA gate and preserves other lock bits; the runtime never resets or disables the shared gate. Bounded snapshots verify disconnected and configured PA8 state.",
      "MCO is programmed before AF attachment. MCO readback failure takes precedence over a final pin configuration mismatch.",
      "Constructor cleanup drops the local Flex before attempting SOURCE disable once, preserving DIV. GPIO-only failure never programs MCO. Observed cleanup booleans are not hardware guarantees.",
      "Normal Drop explicitly disconnects its retained Flex, disables SOURCE, and reads it; subsequent field destruction repeats Flex disconnection. Gate, DIV, ODR and DRIVER remain retained.",
      "mem::forget may leave output active. Reborrowed-token reuse can later occur; active SOURCE prevents new Mco takeover but PA8 reuse can disconnect an orphaned output.",
      "Conditional electrical limits remain 20 MHz, SPEED1, nonzero load <=50 pF, 2.4–5.5 V and -40–105 C; loaded duty/edge requirements, unmeasured source values, source envelope, current and thermal obligations remain explicit."
    ]
  },
